 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
+This property of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` is recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of it; it is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
 
 - The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
+
+## Usage reported to afterModelResponse
+
+The hook's usage argument used to be the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds — so a deployer billing or auditing from this hook under-counted exactly the turns that ran tools (re-cinq/HALEngine#93). It now reports the turn as a whole:
+
+- `afterModelResponse` receives one usage covering every provider call of the turn: a turn driven through two tool rounds is handed the sum of all three calls' tokens, not the final call's ([validated by: sums the usage of every provider call in a turn that ran two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L49)).
+- A round that reports no usage contributes nothing to the total — the sum is never `undefined` or `NaN` because one call stayed silent — and a turn where no provider call reported usage still reports nothing ([validated by: still reports nothing when no round of a tool turn reports usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L80)).
+- The usage's type names what it is — `TurnUsage`, the turn's total across its provider calls — so a reader of the hook signature does not have to open the orchestrator to learn whether it is one call's usage or the turn's ([validated by: types the usage afterModelResponse receives as TurnUsage, the turn total](../../src/orchestration/turnUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L52)).
+- A turn that ran no tools reports exactly what it reported before this change: the single provider call's usage, so the common path does not move ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236), [validated by: keeps the usage an earlier round reported when a later round reports none](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L527)).
